From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: let an older host compiler ignore -Wreturn-mismatch

-Wreturn-mismatch only exists from GCC 14, and -Wno-error=<unknown> is a hard
error, so a pre-14 host compiler stops at scripts/basic/fixdep. The plain
-Wno- form of an unknown warning is silently ignored instead, which keeps the
host flags working on both sides of GCC 14. The target flags are untouched:
the cross compiler is GCC 16.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 968a7aa..7f5107a 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@ HOSTCXXFLAGS = -O2
 
 # GCC 14 rejects by default several things this 2015 tree does throughout.
 # Keep them as warnings; real bugs get fixed in their own patches.
-HOSTCFLAGS   += -fpermissive -Wno-error=return-mismatch -Wno-error=int-conversion -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types
+HOSTCFLAGS   += -fpermissive -Wno-return-mismatch -Wno-error=int-conversion -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types
 
 ifeq ($(HOSTOS),cygwin)
 HOSTCFLAGS	+= -ansi
